{#
  The Google Fonts URL's variable-font ranges (`9..40`, `100..1000`) are written
  as `%2E%2E` and read from src/theme/main.json ("fonts.googleFontsUrl") instead
  of hardcoded here with literal dots: Vite's build-time HTML asset pipeline
  collapses a literal ".." in an href to a single "." (see
  docs/reports/phase-1-skeleton.md), silently truncating the variable range.
  Percent-encoding survives that pass untouched — fonts.googleapis.com decodes
  %2E back to "." itself — and `|raw` keeps Twig from re-escaping the "&"s.
#}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="{{ fonts.googleFontsUrl|raw }}" rel="stylesheet">
